title The room that linked what it shared, bar the one file that mattered
prompt The baton -- audit lap in the grass seat, rotating among Gauge, Civic, Foundations and TAME.
rota lap 4205, row 0 -- Aether, the row that hears; the threshold plus follow-our-compass, the Lindy effect, and the grain and the crossing. What the listen surfaced: the fusion strand "a guard that cannot red guards nothing" reads one step further than the tree had taken it -- a guard proven able to red still guards nothing where its subject sits outside what it reads, which is the shape both this lap's finds wear.
think Opened with fleet_round_open -- clean tree, already on the anointed order, five orphan shelf paths in the dead-letter box, verdict ok. Started the cold roster --scoped in the background rather than full, since the card records three ships taking 1,527s cold on a 4-core pier within one hour.
think The rota read first. Aether asks why the work exists and listens for silence -- the claim a page keeps making, and the place a claim used to stand. The grain page's own fusion strand says a witness must be proven able to make a sound before its silence means anything.
think Took that ear into a TAME sweep of authored Rye for allocations sized by a product of two caller-chosen lengths -- the class a peer had just fenced in mantra/src/diff.rye. image/text_grid.rye came back clean: five render_grid entry points, each checking cols*rows in u64 against qoi.qoi_max_pixels before a pixel is allocated, each refusing GridTooLarge by name. The module is exemplary rather than faulty, and the sweep's honest answer was to say so and move on.
think mand/capabilities.rye was the file the sweep actually surfaced, by a different route: three capabilities.rye paths stand in the tree, linengrow's is a symlink to caravan's, and mand's is a real file whose md5 differs. It publishes neither Refusal nor refusal_reason, privatizes name_slice and label_slice, and its invariant comments drift in nine places.
think Checked first whether this was already known: tools/co/copy_lag_witness.rish reads behind=2 with mand/capabilities.rye named in its ceiling comment. So the drift was counted. What a drift meter cannot do is ask whether the copy needs to exist -- it measures distance and takes the two files as given.
think The room answered that question in its own hand. mand/tally_copy.rye was already a symlink to ../tally/copy.rye, so mand links what it shares everywhere except this one file. Zig refuses an import escaping the root file's directory, which is why a bare-name import is a directory relationship and a symlink is this tree's established answer.
think Proved the link safe before making it: mand uses exactly three symbols -- caps.CapabilityTable, caps.right_read, caps.right_write, plus Capability.init, add_dependent, grant and allows through the table -- and every one stands in caravan's file, which is strictly wider.
think Made the link, ran the three mand ring witnesses and caravan's own capability witness. All four GREEN. The scan then read behind=1, identical=1; lowered behind_ceiling 2 -> 1 with the reason written beside it, and copy_lag_witness came back GREEN over 31 behaviors -- its control reads the ceiling from the law rather than spelling a snapshot, so no control edit was owed.
think Graded what I touched. copy_lag_scan.sh reads A 91 at Meter. mand/README.md read C+ 76 at Door -- reach 30 on 51 words carrying 4 links, 8 cross-refs per 100 words against a budget of 1. That is one frame at depth 1, so I worked it down before resuming.
think A living path molts in place under a cairn, so CHECKPOINTS.md carries the walk-back nib 2883599fe3 first. The rewrite is an accretion: every elder claim kept, plus why the three rings arrive in that order, what they reward, and a table naming the two symlinks. First draft read register 69 -- 31% negative of 16 sentences, over the 20% Door ceiling -- so six clauses were restated to lead with what is. It reads A 92 at 6% negative, reach 100.
obs A drift meter and an existence question are two different readings, and only the first had an instrument. copy_lag has counted mand/capabilities.rye since 20260906 and would have counted it forever; nothing in the tree asked why a room that links two of its three shared modules copies the third.
obs The Door cross-reference budget bit a real page here, and the before-and-after is unusually clean: 51 words with 4 links scored reach 30, and 320 words with the same 4 links score 100. A front door of pure navigation is the exact shape that budget was drawn for.
obs Named rather than taken, for PHEROMONE whose lane the ASCII family is: every ASCII meter in this tree excludes program content by design, and rightly, since converting a fixture byte or a file header changes behavior. The same exclusion swallows printed prose a human reads. A string is data or it is prose, and no meter tells them apart.
obs The card came in at 40,957 of 40,960 -- three bytes free -- so the account went to a shelf and the pin kept a pointer plus the one open question, which is the cairn discipline rather than a trim.
think REDS-FIRST, from the cold roster's own refusal. The scoped cold pass came back `guards_red=3`: `index_row_bound`, `plant`, and `standing_equipment` reading the day's run records. Two were closable on this lap and both were closed on metal.
think `index_row_bound` red on `rows_misordered=1` -- today's shelf carried `20260907.155612` above `20260907.165730`, the %440 class a rebase auto-merge produces. The scan names its own repair, `tools/fixtures/i/index_shelf_repair.sh`; ran it, `repair=sorted`, rescan ok, witness GREEN.
think `plant` red alone rather than in the concurrent-pen family the card blames: the witness asserts `sourcing=13` and the scan reads **14**. The fourteenth is `tools/fixtures/t/topology_partial_control.sh`, born sourcing the plant law at `fb111516c` (`20260907.174056`), three commits back on this tree -- a lane wrote the control correctly and left the floor line behind it. Raised 13 -> 14 with the adopter named and the general lesson written beside it: a floor line is part of the adoption, not a follow-up to it.
think `comment_citation` was red too, outside the three the roster printed, and it is the same shape one room over: `tools/fixtures/c/crushed_index_scan.sh` QUOTED another page's declaration line, `**Kind:** crushed index of [`../../press/`](../../press/)`, and the guard read a quotation as this file's own promise. From `tools/fixtures/c/` that path names `tools/press/`, which stands nowhere. The guard already names *a backticked span illustrates syntax* as an exclusion, so the repair is its own grammar: backticks, no link, with the reason written in. `crushed_index_witness` stays GREEN across the edit.
obs Both closures are one shape: a guard reading a MENTION as a PROMISE. A grep for a path counts the sentence that says the opposite -- which is exactly the finding a peer booked at `20260907.153124` for the plant scan's own adoption reading, met here from the receiving end in a second house. That is a lantern firing twice.
think A fourth red fell after the hot pass: `dated_spelling` refused `tools/fixtures/l/living_prose_roster.sh` for a dated pattern demanding a sprig. The exclusion means ONE page and named it by its sprig, so the repair is the literal path rather than a looser date class -- 520 roster paths before and after, and living_docs_lint GREEN across it.
think Then the same shape bit the repair itself: my comment QUOTED the elder pattern to explain the fix, and the guard refused the tree for prose about its own repair. Described rather than quoted, GREEN. That is the third house on this lap for one defect.
think The roster's own record went on naming `comment_citation` and `dated_spelling` red after both read GREEN on metal, because both are `tier cadence` and their newest rows dated from a `20260907.101056` cadence pass. A repaired cadence guard keeps its stale verdict until something re-runs it; the runner takes a bare guard name for exactly that, so `standing_equipment_run.sh --hot <guard>` refreshed each row and `runs_red` fell 5 -> 3.
think THE REBASE, and the one withdrawal. xy moved nine commits under this lap; `tools/p/plant_witness.rish` conflicted, and upstream's side had removed the spelled floor entirely -- the witness reads `adoption_floor_held=yes` from the scan now, so a lane that adopts passes free and only a control that LOST its import refuses. That removes the class where my raise reset its counter. Took theirs whole and withdrew mine; the card, the shelf and this log all say so. It is the structural form of the very sentence I had written as a habit, which is the honest way to lose a race.
think The post-rebase re-verify found `index_row_bound` red again, and this time it was NOT my rebase: `git show xy/main:session-logs/date/README-index-20260907.md` carries the same three duplicate stamps -- `20260907.182550`, `.192800`, `.192817` -- so a peer's rebase published a shelf with each row standing twice. `index_shelf_repair.sh` refuses a duplicate on purpose (which of two rows to lift is a hand's call) and sorts once the pairs are gone. Each pair was byte-identical, so the call was free; lifted the later of each, re-sorted 108 rows, witness GREEN.
obs Three reds stand and are named rather than taken -- `dated_path`, `season_leaf_choir`, `two_rooms_doorway`. Each is larger than a bounded frame, and the doorway census is already on the card and in the baton. `standing_equipment` reads roster_broken while they stand, which it also did at my open.
obs A lantern that fires twice becomes a loom, and this one has fired three times in one lap plus once for a peer at `20260907.145907`. What a loom for it would read -- a guard telling a live pattern from a described one -- is left as the open question rather than built, since a wrong answer would teach every guard to skip its own documentation.
obs A process fault of my own, recorded: the cold pass ran in the background while I edited, so it closed `tree_moved=yes`. The cold open's job is to prove a clean open, which `fleet_round_open.sh` and a clean `git status` did independently; the hot pass is what measures the tree the commit ships.
